{
  "title": "Namaz of Lady Fatimah Zehra (s.a.)",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "سُبْحَانَ ذِي الْعِزِّ الشَّامِخِ الْمُنِيْفِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL I'ZZISH SHAAMIKHIL MUNEEF\nGlory be to the Lord of lofty and exalted might!\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْجَلَالِ الْبَاذِخِ الْعَظِيْمِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL JALAALIL BAADHIKHIL A'ZEEM\nGlory be to the Lord of sublime and immense majesty!\nسُبْحَانَ ذِي الْمُلْكِ الْفَاخِرِ الْقَدِيْمِ\nSUBHAANA DHIL MULKIL FAAKHIRIL QADEEM\nGlory be to the Lord of grand and eternal dominion!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَّرٰى اَثَرَ النَّمْلَةِ فِي الصَّفَا\nSUBHAANA MAY YARAA ATHARAN NAMLATI FIS SAFAA\nGlory be to Him Who sees the footstep of the ant on the smooth stone!\nسُبْحَانَ مَنْ يَّرٰى وَقْعَ الطَّيْرِ فِي الْهَوَآءِ\nSUBHAANA MAY YARAA WAQ'AT TAYRI FIL HAWAAA'\nGlory be to Him Who sees the bird's flight in the air!",
  "merits": "It is narrated that Lady Fatimah al-Zahra' (s.a.) used to offer a two-unit prayer taught by Archangel Gabriel. In the first unit, recite Surah al-Fatihah and repeat Surah al-Qadr one hundred times. In the second unit, recite Surah al-Fatihah and repeat Surah al-Tawhid one hundred times. After the taslim, say this litany:"
